# AETHER NEXUS — environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the repository root and fill in the value.
# `.env` is read by server/chat-server.js with a tiny built-in parser (no dotenv
# dependency). Real shell/CI environment variables always take precedence.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# The game runs fully offline without any of this. If ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is
# absent the chat server answers {"type":"error","message":"no-key"} and the
# in-game chat box falls back to a local persona-driven response generator,
# showing a small "offline persona" badge in the chat header.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required for live AI dialogue
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Anthropic API key used to generate NPC dialogue.
# Create one at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys
# Never commit the filled-in .env — keep the key out of version control.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional overrides
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Port for the local dialogue server. The client also probes
# http://127.0.0.1:8787/api/chat directly, so change this only if you also add a
# matching Vite dev-server proxy for /api.
# CHAT_PORT=8787

# Model used for NPC replies. Streamed, capped at ~150 output tokens so replies
# read like in-game barks rather than essays.
# CHAT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
